{"id":8744,"date":"2022-10-19T10:02:20","date_gmt":"2022-10-19T17:02:20","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=8744"},"modified":"2025-10-23T13:33:23","modified_gmt":"2025-10-23T20:33:23","slug":"2-7-functions-cde-blockly","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/2-7-functions-cde-blockly\/","title":{"rendered":"2.7: Functions"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213687c73f\" name=\"6a2213687c73f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>We've Moved!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text css=&#8221;.vc_custom_1761251600046{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}&#8221;]<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignleft wp-image-11766\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/06\/icon_warning-150x150-2-84x85.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"81\" height=\"82\" \/><\/p>\n<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\"><strong>We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: <a href=\"http:\/\/learn.robolink.com\">Robolink Learn<\/a>! Lessons here will remain available until the end of June 2026. This version of Basecamp will no longer be updated and uses outdated references to Blockly for Robolink. You can access the previous version of <a href=\"https:\/\/codrone.robolink.com\/edu\/blockly-archive\/\">Blockly here<\/a>.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213687c86e\" name=\"6a2213687c86e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What are Functions?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><strong>Functions<\/strong> are a way to save time and energy by storing commonly used blocks of code in one named set. For a real-world example, when you\u2019re drinking a glass of water, the entire task might look like this:<\/span><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Find glass<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Bring over to water source<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pour water into glass<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Make sure water doesn\u2019t overflow!<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Drink water<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">But instead of announcing all the steps you&#8217;ll take, you could just say you\u2019re drinking water! Functions work the same way. Multiple lines of code can be included in one function that you name and set up to be used in your program.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213687c8d5\" name=\"6a2213687c8d5\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Defining a Function<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To define a function, or explain what is going to be in it, you will need the <strong>to do something<\/strong> block in the pink &#8220;Functions&#8221; menu. Drag that to your workspace and then name your function in the white box. This should be something memorable that describes your function well. Next, drag the blocks you need into the function. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;8772&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try it now! Make a function that has the name \u201cpushup\u201d and that has your CoDrone EDU do a push-up. It should take off, hover, and land. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;720&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_single_image image=&#8221;721&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213687c92a\" name=\"6a2213687c92a\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Using a Function<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Once you define a function, you should see a block for it in the &#8220;Functions&#8221; menu. To use it, drag it into your workspace and drop it to wherever you would like to see it in your program.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><em>Remember your very first challenge with CoDrone EDU?<\/em> You needed to see how many drone pushups you could do. Try doing this now with a loop and your new function!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10289&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213687c979\" name=\"6a2213687c979\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Functions in Flight<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To use a function in your flight program, drag its <strong>function<\/strong> block to where you would like to see it in your code.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try this out now! After your CoDrone EDU does a few drone pushups, have it take off, pitch forward at 100% power for 1 second, and then land.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;10290&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213687cb15\" name=\"6a2213687cb15\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Warning<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you plan on using your function later on, do not remove it from your workspace! Doing this will delete the entire function, and you will not be able to locate it in the &#8220;Functions&#8221; menu. The first image shows the function appearing in the menu. The second image shows the function disappearing from the menu if the workspace is cleared.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-8775\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/10\/Screen-Shot-2022-11-06-at-4.17.09-PM-300x197.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"474\" height=\"311\" srcset=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/10\/Screen-Shot-2022-11-06-at-4.17.09-PM-300x197.png 300w, https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/10\/Screen-Shot-2022-11-06-at-4.17.09-PM-1024x672.png 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 474px) 100vw, 474px\" \/><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone wp-image-8776\" src=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/10\/Screen-Shot-2022-11-06-at-4.17.27-PM-300x209.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"445\" height=\"310\" srcset=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/10\/Screen-Shot-2022-11-06-at-4.17.27-PM-300x209.png 300w, https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/10\/Screen-Shot-2022-11-06-at-4.17.27-PM-1024x714.png 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 445px) 100vw, 445px\" \/>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213687cb7f\" name=\"6a2213687cb7f\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: Initialize<\/b><\/p>\n<p>Write functions so that CoDrone EDU can fly in your name\u2019s initials! Start with the initial for your first name and the initial for your last name, and then use them in a flight program. To simplify the letters, try <em>writing<\/em> the letters in block-style with straight lines instead of curved paths.[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;8777&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213687cbce\" name=\"6a2213687cbce\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Lesson Complete<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]In this lesson, you learned how to write more efficient code by grouping commands into functions. Functions are defined and then can be used in your program![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;7547&#8243; img_size=&#8221;750&#215;670&#8243; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 We've Moved! [vc_column_text css=\".vc_custom_1761251600046{padding-top: 20px !important;padding-right: 20px !important;padding-bottom: 20px !important;padding-left: 20px !important;background-color: #ffdddd !important;border-radius: 3px !important;}\"] We\u2019ve moved to our new lesson portal: Robolink Learn! Lessons here&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/2-7-functions-cde-blockly\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":4739,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":3877,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1746,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,167,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2108,4328,14401,2131,2122,2126],"class_list":["post-8744","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-cde","lesson-tag-cdej","lesson-tag-functions","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-senior","module-intermediate","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/8744","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":21,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/8744\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":13629,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/8744\/revisions\/13629"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/4739"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=8744"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=8744"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=8744"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}